420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 70 0 R
/T (Both demo APIs showed the most common API weakness: data can be read without logging in, and the open design makes it easy to collect records one by one. JSONPlaceholder also echoed any website origin with credentials allowed and accepted empty input, while Restful-Booker published default credentials and supports Basic authentication. These are expected for practice APIs, but each would be a serious issue on a real service. The fixes are mostly design choices: require authentication, return less data, check access per record, and validate input.)
/E (Both demo APIs showed the most common API weakness: data can be read without logging in, and the open design makes it easy to collect records one by one. JSONPlaceholder also echoed any website origin with credentials allowed and accepted empty input, while Restful-Booker published default credentials and supports Basic authentication. These are expected for practice APIs, but each would be a serious issue on a real service. The fixes are mostly design choices: require authentication, return less data, check access per record, and validate input.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
